# Observability Conventions

Logging and observability for every backend stack in one file (IAN-381). The rules are the same in every language and live in `CLAUDE.md` as R-341 to R-346: one request ID per request, one structured logger, analytics only through the event registry, no swallowed errors, health endpoints, and instrumented outbound calls. Each section below gives one stack's form of those rules. The stack track files (`CLAUDE-PYTHON.md`, `CLAUDE-BACKEND.md`, `CLAUDE-GO.md`, `CLAUDE-RUBY.md`) keep their section headings and point here, so this file loads on the same paths they do.

